  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Plan Sverige EU-ECHO Nigeria 2018-2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plan Sweden EU-ECHO Nigeria 2018-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Plan International Sverige har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering av egeninsats om 3 540 437 SEK f&#xf6;r ECHO-projektet &quot;Responding to the urgent education and protection needs of children and adolescent boys and girls affected by the conflict in Northeast Nigeria&quot; under perioden 2018-2020. 

Insatsen syftar till att ge flickor och pojkar i &#xe5;ldrarna 6-17 &#xe5;r i nord&#xf6;stra Nigeria tillg&#xe5;ng till relevant formell och icke-formell utbildning i en humanit&#xe4;r kontext och skydd mot v&#xe5;ld, exploatering och f&#xf6;rsummelse genom f&#xf6;rebyggande och responsbaserade aktiviteter. 

Insatsen har en total budget p&#xe5; 2 941 176 EUR, vilket motsvarar cirka 31 764 701 SEK. S&#xf6;kt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida &#xe4;r 3 540 437 SEK, vilket motsvarar cirka 9 procent av den totala budgeten.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plan International Sverige has applied to Sida for funding of 3 540 437 SEK to carry out the ECHO-project &quot;Responding to the urgent education and protection needs of children and adolescent boys and girls affected by the conflict in Northeast Nigeria&quot; during the period 2018-2020.

The purpose of the action is to provide girls and boys between the ages of 6-17 in Northeast Nigeria access to relevant formal and non-formal learning opportunities in a humanitarian context and protection aganinst violence, abuse, exploitation and neglect through prevention and response activities.

The contribution&apos;s total budget is 2 941 176 EUR, corresponding to approximately 31 764 701 SEK. The requested support from Sida is 3 540 437 SEK, which corresponds to approximately 9 per cent of the total budget.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Principal objective:
Girls and boys affected by the crisis in Northeast Nigeria access quality, relevant formal and non-formal learning opportunities in emergencies contexts and are protected from violence, abuse, exploitation and neglect through prevention and response activities
Specific objective:
Girls and boys have increased access to quality formal and non-formal learning opportunities and live in a protective environment in which children, families and communities have skills, knowledge and behaviours to identify risks, and prevent and respond to protection concerns in Borno State Nigeria.
Result 1: Targeted boys and girls ages 6-17 years access quality, relevant formal primary and secondart education learning opportunities.
Result 2: Targeted girls and boys aged 9 - 17 years access quality, relevant nonformal learning opportunities
Result 3: At-risk girls and boys have access to school- and community-based child protection prevention and response services and psychosocial support.</narrative>
  </description>
